#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# resultant

#% text
# `resultant(p, q, x)` gives the resultant of the polynomials `p` and `q` with respect to `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The resultant is the determinant of the Sylvester matrix; it is 0 exactly when `p` and `q` have a common root in `x` (or both leading coefficients vanish). Other symbols are parameters.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
resultant(x^2 - 1, x - 1, x)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
resultant(x^2 - 1, x - 2, x)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
resultant(x^2 + a*x + 1, x - b, x)
#% output
#= 1 + a*b + b^2

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Eliminating `x` from two equations gives a condition on `y`:

#% cell
resultant(x^2 + y^2 - 1, x - y, x)
#% output
#= -1 + 2*y^2

#% text
# The polynomial of `sqrt(2) + sqrt(3)`, by eliminating `y` from `y^2 = 2` and `(x - y)^2 = 3`:

#% cell
expand(resultant(y^2 - 2, (x - y)^2 - 3, y))
#% output
#= 1 - 10*x^2 + x^4

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The resultant of `p` and its derivative is the discriminant up to a factor:

#% cell
p = x^3 - 2*x + 1; [resultant(p, d(p, x), x), discriminant(p, x)]
#% output
#= [-5, 5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `discriminant`, `eliminate`, `polynomial_gcd`, `groebner_basis`
